= Questions of Strategy

The coalition is pulled between different strategic instincts. What should be the primary emphasis of our approach right now?

[? if strategic_emphasis != 0 : We have previously emphasized a [+ strategic_emphasis +] approach. Changing course now will likely have drawbacks. ?]

- @insurgent_approach: Primary unfriendly incumbents and build independent movement infrastructure - the party should fear us.
- @progressive_approach: Win the argument and legislate structural change through the party as it exists.
- @labor_approach: Work through organized labor to win material gains for working people.
- @establishment_approach: Hold the coalition together and win elections first; ideology second.
- @easy_discard

@insurgent_approach
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.strategic_emphasis && Q.strategic_emphasis != "insurgent") {
    Q.emphasis_changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: emphasis_changed if emphasis_changed = 1
on-departure: strategic_emphasis = "insurgent"; insurgent_strength += 10; dirty_break_support += 1; insurgent_dissent -= 5; establishment_dem_dissent += 3; gop_estab_relation -= 3;

The insurgent wing pushes a course of primary challenges and independent organizing, betting that fear of a challenge from the left is the only thing that moves the party's center of gravity.

@progressive_approach
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.strategic_emphasis && Q.strategic_emphasis != "progressive") {
    Q.emphasis_changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: emphasis_changed if emphasis_changed = 1
on-departure: strategic_emphasis = "progressive"; progressive_strength += 10; progressive_dissent -= 10; insurgent_dissent -= 5; establishment_dem_dissent -= 5;

The progressive wing argues for winning the intellectual argument and legislating structural change - a public option, antitrust enforcement, campaign finance reform - through the party as it already exists.

@labor_approach
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.strategic_emphasis && Q.strategic_emphasis != "labor_left") {
    Q.emphasis_changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: emphasis_changed if emphasis_changed = 1
on-departure: strategic_emphasis = "labor_left"; labor_left_strength += 10; jobs_program += 1; labor_left_dissent -= 5; union_density += 0.3;

The labor-left wing argues that organizing workplaces and winning material gains through the labor movement is worth more than any number of primary challenges or floor speeches.

@establishment_approach
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.strategic_emphasis && Q.strategic_emphasis != "establishment_dem") {
    Q.emphasis_changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: emphasis_changed if emphasis_changed = 1
on-departure: strategic_emphasis = "establishment_dem"; establishment_dem_strength += 10; coalition_dissent -= 1; establishment_dem_dissent -= 10; insurgent_dissent -= 5; gop_estab_relation += 5; blue_dog_dissent -= 5;

The establishment wing argues the priority has to be holding the existing coalition together and winning the next election - ideological battles can wait.

@emphasis_changed
on-arrival: insurgent_dissent += 5; progressive_dissent += 5; labor_left_dissent += 5; establishment_dem_dissent += 5; blue_dog_dissent += 5;

Shifting our strategic emphasis again leaves parts of the coalition feeling whiplashed.
